## Route through numbered hints

Exercise files: [ex01.lp](../assets/seeknumbers/instances/ex01.lp) · [seeknumbers.lp](../assets/seeknumbers/seeknumbers.lp) · [ex01.json](../assets/seeknumbers/solutions/ex01.json).

```elixir
workdir = Course.workspace(Path.expand("../assets/seeknumbers", __DIR__))
```

Build a directed orthogonal path from the white marker to the black marker through every other cell exactly once. It must not intersect itself. Before the first numbered cell it is straight; after a numbered cell, count exactly that many bends before the next number or the finish.

Complete the starter encoding before comparing its projected models with the supplied solution data.

### Keep the data contract

Read `cell/2`, `first/2`, `final/2` and `hint/3`. Show path edges through `path/4`. Local predecessor/successor constraints need a connectivity condition to exclude disconnected cycles.

### Develop and check the encoding

Complete the editable encoding below. Compare its shown atom sets with the JSON answers in `solutions`; `optimal_cost` records a proven optimum when present. Download your edits before cleanup.

```elixir
Course.archive(workdir, "seeknumbers.zip")
```

```elixir
~S"""
#show path/4.
"""
|> Clingo.solve!(files: [Path.join(workdir, "instances/ex01.lp")], models: :all)
|> Course.display()
```

### Check boundary cases

Test the smallest instance first, then check each derived relation. Compare projected model sets and, when optimizing, proven costs.

